<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg k_sigma at 1.12 µm in the E. rowelli ocellus (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg calibration (a=0.12, b=0.88, Du=1, Dv=22, γ=34122.25342711872, seed 3223, λ=1.12 µm, age 0 Ma). Dispersion Pearson r stays 0.9915 (RMSE 1171, KS 0.069). The saturated wavenumber is now a parabolic sub-bin DCT peak at 14.072 cycles, so λ_2d = 1.114 µm (0.5% under 1.12 µm; Pass 1's integer ring said 1.100 µm). In-band controls separate: full mode +8571, equal diffusion −5662, reversed ratio −22114. Specimen-versus-last-frame 12-bin orientation L1 is 0.0134, not zero. GIF unchanged at 12 frames and 640×480; CV similarity 96.0. Overall 87.2/100 (faithfulness 86.9, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 506526 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 c75a57997907af22c3bddaa161e2ae336cea5da5d5b7a7a25f24ba4e4453800e (sha256 c75a57997907af22c3bddaa161e2ae336cea5da5d5b7a7a25f24ba4e4453800e), spec_fingerprint 345373ab42e0e02cf6b6faa2dc71e527f6cadf8f798b162c003fe87164eb8759. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 345373ab42e0e02cf6b6faa2dc71e527f6cadf8f798b162c003fe87164eb8759; artifact_sha256: c75a57997907af22c3bddaa161e2ae336cea5da5d5b7a7a25f24ba4e4453800e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0/euperipatoides_rowelli_specimen.jpg=29166a767a52ae55..., datasets/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=953c4f019dafd397..., datasets/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=4bc7e5b005ed9e1a...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics du/dt = a − u + u²v, dv/dt = b − u²v. | E. rowelli ocelli are about 100 µm across, with screening pigment and a rhabdom of microvilli (Mayer 2006; Kirwan 2018; Ljungholm & Nilsson 2021). | Photoreceptor centres are about 2.5 µm apart. Kirwan 2018 figures microvilli with a 1 µm scale bar.; reconstructed_in_script: γ is solved so argmax σ(k) = 2π × 14. Sub-bin DCT power peaks at 14.072 cycles (1.114 µm). | In-band max Re σ is +8571 (full), −5662 (Du = Dv), and −22114 (Dv < Du). | Orientation-histogram L1 between the Couch photograph and the GIF last frame is 0.0134. | N = 89 detail wavelengths across a 100 µm eye at 0 Ma, versus N = 0 below a 10 µm Cambrian floor.; transfer_boundary: 1.12 µm is the assigned detail scale, not a Turing wavelength measured by those papers. | The 15.68 µm patch is magnified onto the body mask for display. Macroscopic annuli are not assigned period 1.12 µm.; does_not_claim: That the 0.5% residual between 1.114 µm and 1.12 µm is zero. | That the Couch photograph is an electron micrograph at 1.12 µm. | A successor chronospecies, or a second assessor. | Cryptographic nanopub signatures (no local nanopub profile).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=2.5]: Still one assessor. No second provider was available in this run.",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor — still open. This run had only the builder-assessor.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved: sub-bin peak is 14.072 cycles, λ = 1.114 µm.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Resolved: orientation-histogram L1 = 0.0134 against a null of 0.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Resolved: in-band controls are +8571, −5662, and −22114.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.72e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

